---
import Section from './Section.astro';
// The honest conversion surface. The Flutter app is NOT shipped, so there is no
// download button and no waitlist form posting into a void. What is real today is
// the self-hostable backend — so that is the call to action, plainly labelled.
---

<Section
  n="10"
  id="self-host"
  tone="sunk"
  labelledby="selfhost-h"
  note="No app-store buttons, no fake waitlist. The mobile app is Phase 2, and we won’t pretend otherwise."
>
  <p class="eyebrow rise">Get started</p>
  <h2 id="selfhost-h" class="rise mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,2.9rem)]">
    There&rsquo;s no app to download yet &mdash; but the whole backend is yours to run.
  </h2>

  <div class="mt-10 grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.95fr_1.05fr] lg:gap-16">
    <div class="rise">
      <p class="lede">
        The backend is complete, deployed, and multi-tenant. The mobile app is the next phase, and
        until it ships, public sign-ups stay closed.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
        Healthee runs on a single small VPS. The database is never exposed to the internet; the API
        is reachable only through nginx over TLS; a nightly off-box backup is one command. You keep
        every byte.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rise">
      <figure
        class="surface code-win"
        aria-label="Self-hosting: clone, configure, and bring up the stack"
      >
        <figcaption class="code-bar">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="flex gap-1.5">
            <span class="code-dot"></span><span class="code-dot"></span><span class="code-dot"></span>
          </span>
          <span class="mono ml-2 text-xs">self-host &middot; single VPS</span>
        </figcaption>
        <pre><code><span class="text-ink-faint"># clone your fork and configure secrets</span>
git clone <span class="text-accent-soft">&lt;your-fork&gt;</span> ~/healthee &amp;&amp; cd ~/healthee
cp infra/.env.example infra/.env

<span class="text-ink-faint"># bring up the stack — TimescaleDB stays internal-only</span>
docker compose -f infra/docker/docker-compose.prod.yml up -d db
docker compose run --rm api python -m healthee.db.migrate
docker compose -f infra/docker/docker-compose.prod.yml up -d api scheduler

<span class="text-ink-faint"># verify</span>
curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:8765/healthz   <span class="text-accent-soft">→ &#123;"status":"ok","db":"ok"&#125;</span></code></pre>
      </figure>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-soft">
        <span class="mono text-ink-faint">Next:</span> follow the build. When sign-ups open, this is
        where they&rsquo;ll open.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>
